repository-code: "https://github.com/jsilvao/walsh-hadamard-explicit-rate"
abstract: >-
  Paper and Lean 4 development. Over every field of characteristic zero,
  the Walsh–Hadamard transform on N = 2^k points has binary linear circuits
  with C(H^{⊗k}) ≤ 2^k · √(k+1) · 2^{Φ(n)} gates for every k, where
  n = ⌊log₂(k+1)⌋ and Φ(n) = 400·√((n+2)·log₂(n+2)), that is,
  N (log N)^{1/2 + O(√(log log log N / log log N))}. This makes explicit the
  o(1) in OpenAI's N (log N)^{1/2+o(1)} for this transform. The proof
  sharpens one level of OpenAI's template, makes the work outside recursive
  calls polynomial in the number of queries (character checks on the two
  Hamming tails with a polynomial decoder, and a row-diagonal routing
  pencil), and lets the template grow with N. The paper also proves limits
  of the method. Every theorem, proposition, lemma and corollary is
  machine-checked in Lean 4 (143 results, standard axioms only).
keywords:
  - Walsh–Hadamard transform
  - linear circuits
  - fast Fourier transform
  - Lean
  - formal verification
